    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0140a89_c2404406",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000451
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T17:40:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, can we get away from this?  Does the carrier really need to kow if I\u0027m bluetooth tethering or not?\n\nIn the existing call paths this type comes back to us and we use it to tell which interfaces to start.  But in this call that\u0027s not the case, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2198,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2198,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "8e683cbe4630ef204ce14e69713519a39f86eb77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90f23217_1db9479a",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T18:41:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Erik, is it a good idea to perpetuate these TETHERING_xxx types in the long term, or are we trying to move away from them? If the latter, is there another abstraction that we should consider here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2198,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2198,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "8e683cbe4630ef204ce14e69713519a39f86eb77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "167f1a91_3c164bef",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080048
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T20:36:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just realized I didn\u0027t reply on this comment thread, but I actually don\u0027t think it\u0027s possible to remove this right now because it\u0027s used by provisioning apps and carriers actually do seem to care which type is being used. For example, AT\u0026T has a different url for the provisioning check with wifi than for usb and bluetooth.",
      "parentUuid": "90f23217_1db9479a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2198,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2198,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "8e683cbe4630ef204ce14e69713519a39f86eb77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9c4922e_e80ddb97",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000451
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-29T20:49:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sigh.  We should deprecate that.  Maybe in future we can just ignore the passed in |type| and instead send along -1.",
      "parentUuid": "167f1a91_3c164bef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2198,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2198,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "8e683cbe4630ef204ce14e69713519a39f86eb77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
